# webpeek targets file
#
# One target per line. A target may be a hostname, an IP, or a URL (a URL limits
# the web tools to that exact URL). Blank lines and anything after '#' are
# ignored. A line may end with the flag `prod` to scan that host at reduced
# "production" intensity (nmap --max-rate 100, nuclei -rl 20, ffuf -rate 20,
# WPScan --throttle 500).
#
# This list IS the allow-list: the active tools only ever touch what is named
# here, and any redirect off to a host not on the list is refused. There is no
# engagement-window check - authorisation for the engagement lives in the
# contract, and this file is your record of what that contract permits. Keep it
# under change control (e.g. in the engagement repo) if you want an audit trail.
#
# Run with:  sudo ./webpeek.py --targets targets.txt
#
# Example (delete these and add your own):

app.example.com            prod       # live customer-facing app
api.example.com            prod
staging.example.com                   # non-production, full intensity
https://portal.example.com/app        # web tools limited to this URL

# A bare CIDR range is containment-only: it is never scanned itself, but a
# redirect into it during the CSP fetch is allowed. Name the hosts you want
# scanned individually above.
# 10.0.0.0/24
